    "title": "Artemis II astronauts splash down after NASA's mission around the moon",
    "text": "SPACEArtemis II astronauts splash down after NASA moon flyby Brooke EdwardsFlorida TodayApril 10, 2026Updated April 11, 2026, 8:51 a.m. ETNASA’s Artemis II mission has come to an end, splashing down Friday night, April 10, after a historic lunar flyby, bringing its four astronauts safely back on Earth.The Orion spacecraft blazed through the atmosphere at a maximum speed of 23,864 mph, the outside reaching toasty temperatures upward of 5,000 degrees, before floating down into the Pacific Ocean under three main orange and white parachutes. Splashdown occurred at 8:07 p.m. EDT Friday, April 10 off the coast of San Diego, California.",
